s so there's 60 minutes in one hour  minutes are cancelling numerator nanamia  we were left with hours but we want days  so we say there's 24 hours per one day  and again you can see the units are  canceling numerator denominator you may  try tit this way you say okay wait a  second you know I have to flip it over  because I want those units to cancel so  you'll know you've set it up right as  long as these are equal 24 hours is  equal to one day you're not changing the  value of the fraction you're just  changing the way that it looks you're  just changing the units okay so let's  just see we're left with meters  per day so all you have left to do is  multiply 8 x 1 x 60 x 24 and then 1 x  100 x 1 x 1 ok that's the denominator  and then divide those two and you're  gonna get the number of meters per day  meters / days so I hope you're enjoying  this video I hope you learn something go  ahead and subscribe to the channel check  out some of my past videos and I've got  some more videos like these coming so  stay tuned and I'll talk to you soon

